# MC-B-F5. L §5.16: "A query that has no closed form is a statistic over paths: it stands only in an ask line that
# states paths N seed S"; low_w is random through w's balances (E §3.1 step 10), and no fact is read in it directly
# in an affine form, so mean(low_w) on a line without paths has no closed form (LOAD-RANDOM, E §3.1 step 10). snap8
# called low_w not random (a query is asked of a random value).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
source s "s"
index delays = 1..10
place w: accounts DUK lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..
input amt: money DUK question "amount?"
version o
  cite s
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[w] = 0.00 DUK at 2026-01-01 start
  amt = 100.00 DUK governs always "a"
def delay[m in months]: dist = discrete(1 for k in delays)
def low_w: money DUK = min(bal(w, end_of(m) - 1) for m in months)
move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on add_days(start_of(m), delay[m])
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to w amount amt
ask q5: mean(low_w) law 2026-12-31
=== expect
refused: LOAD-RANDOM mean(low_w) has no closed form; state paths N seed S ...
